const READINGS = {
1:[
"My name is Jim Hawkins. My friends, Doctor Livesey and Squire Trelawney, asked me to write the story of our adventures on Treasure Island. So I will pick up my pen and begin.",
"When I was a boy, I lived with my father and mother at the Admiral Benbow Inn. It was a lonely place, near the cliffs and the sea.",
"One day a tall, strong sailor came to our door. He had a large sea chest with him. His coat was old and dirty, his skin was brown from the sun, and he had a scar on one cheek. He sang part of an old sea song: “Fifteen men on the dead man’s chest — Yo-ho-ho and a bottle of rum!”",
"Then he asked my father for a glass of rum. “Do many people stay here?” he asked.",
"“No,” said my father, “business is bad.”",
"“Then this is the place for me! I’ll stay here for a time. You can call me captain. All I want is bacon and eggs and rum.” He threw some gold coins on the table.",
"He was a silent man. He often watched the sea through a telescope. In the evenings he sat alone with a glass of rum. Every day he walked on the cliffs, and when he came back he asked, “Did any sailors come here today?”",
"He gave me a little money every month. “You must promise to look for a sailor with one leg, boy,” he said. “Tell me immediately if you see him.” The captain was afraid when he said this. Sometimes I had terrible dreams about the man with one leg.",
"The captain often got drunk. He sang sea songs loudly and made the other customers sing with him. The house shook with the noise. He told terrible stories about pirates who robbed and killed innocent people. My father was worried and became ill. “Nobody will come to drink at the inn while he is here,” he said.",
"The captain stayed for weeks but he never paid any more money. My parents were afraid to ask him.",
"But one person from the village was not afraid of the captain. That was Doctor Livesey. He came to see my father, and then he waited for his horse downstairs. The captain was in the same room. Suddenly he began to sing.",
"Doctor Livesey continued talking to a friend while the captain sang. The old sailor banged his hand angrily on the table. Everyone was quiet except the doctor.",
"“Silence! I’m singing!” shouted the captain.",
"“Are you speaking to me?” asked Doctor Livesey. “I have only one thing to say to you. If you drink rum all the time, you will soon die!”",
"The captain was very angry. He took out a knife and threatened the doctor.",
"“Put the knife back in your pocket, you dirty man,” said the doctor. “If you don’t, you will hang next week.”",
"The two men looked at each other. Then the sailor put down the knife and sat at the table.",
"“I am not only a doctor. I am also a magistrate,” said Doctor Livesey. “You will go to prison if you behave like this again.” Then he left the inn, got on his horse and rode back to the village."
],
2:[
"One cold day in January the captain went to the beach. While he was out, a sailor came to the inn. I noticed that two fingers were missing on his left hand.",
"“Is Bill here?” he asked.",
"“No,” I replied. “The captain is our only guest.”",
"“What does he look like?” he asked.",
"“He has a scar on one cheek. He’s walking on the beach.”",
"“That’s Bill,” said the man. “I’ll wait for him.” He pulled me with him into the inn and hid behind the door. He had a long sword and he rested his hand on it. He was very nervous.",
"At last the captain returned.",
"“Bill!” said the man. “Black Dog!” said the captain.",
"They sat together in the inn and drank rum while they talked secretly. Suddenly they began to quarrel. They took out their swords and fought. The captain was very angry and Black Dog ran out of the inn and disappeared. But the captain fell unconscious on the ground.",
"My mother and I tried to help him. My father was very ill, so Doctor Livesey, who was at the inn to see my father, looked at the captain. “It’s his heart,” he said.",
"We carried the captain to his bed. There was a tattoo on his arm: ‘Billy Bones.’",
"“Where’s Black Dog?” he asked when he woke.",
"“He’s not here,” said the doctor. “But you will die if you drink more rum, Mister Billy Bones. You must go to bed and rest for a week.”",
"The captain stayed in his bed. “Remember, boy! Tell me if you see a sailor with one leg,” he said. “They are all pirates from the ship of Captain Flint. They want to steal my sea chest. They will give me the black spot.”",
"“What’s the black spot?” I asked. “It’s the sign of the pirates,” he whispered.",
"Next day my father died. I forgot everything about Black Dog and the black spot. But one day a blind man came to the Admiral Benbow. He tapped on the road with his stick. His clothes were old and he looked terrible. “Take me to the captain, boy,” he said.",
"“I can’t,” I said. He twisted my arm cruelly. He forced me to lead him to the room of Billy Bones.",
"As soon as the captain saw him, his face went white with fear. “Blind Pew!” he said.",
"“Hold out your hand,” said Pew. He put something in the captain’s hand. Then he went downstairs and left the inn. Tap! Tap! Tap!",
"Billy Bones looked at the small black circle on the paper in his hand. There was writing on the other side: ‘10 o’clock’. He tried to stand up, but suddenly he made a strange noise. He fell to the floor. He was dead!",
"I called my mother and told her everything. “If the blind man comes back with the pirates, he will kill us,” we thought. We went to the village for help, but everyone was afraid.",
"“The captain didn’t pay for his room and food,” said my mother. “He owes us a lot of money. Let’s go back to the inn and take it.”",
"It was dark now. We walked through the night and went into the Admiral Benbow. We were alone in the house with the body of the dead captain. We went upstairs and opened his sea chest. We found old clothes, some tropical shells, and a bundle of papers. Under all this, there were hundreds of foreign coins. My mother began to count them.",
"“Let’s go quickly,” I said. “No,” she said. “I want to be honest. I will take enough to pay for what he owes and nothing more.”",
"At that moment I heard a noise outside. Tap! Tap! Tap! It was the blind pirate!",
"I took the papers, my mother took some of the money, and we ran out of the inn and hid behind the trees by the road.",
"Soon I saw three men in the moonlight. They went inside the inn. “Somebody stole things from the sea chest. There’s nothing,” one of the men told Blind Pew.",
"“They must be near here,” said Blind Pew. “Find them!”",
"The pirates began to look for us. But then we heard horses. Immediately the pirates ran away in all directions. Pew stood in the road. “Don’t leave me,” he cried.",
"Five men on horseback came over the hill. The blind man was still on the road. The first rider tried to stop but Blind Pew fell under his horse and was dead. The riders were the Customs officers."
],
3:[
"Someone from the village told the officers about the pirates and they came to rescue us.",
"“What did they want?” one of them wondered. “What did Mister Billy Bones hide in his sea chest?”",
"“I’ve got some papers,” I said.",
"One took me back to Doctor Livesey’s house to recover, while the other men helped my mother. The doctor was at the table with Squire Trelawney. They both wanted to look at the papers.",
"“Captain Flint was a famous pirate,” said Doctor Livesey. “He stole gold and silver from ships in the West Indies. After he died, nobody could find his treasure. But maybe Captain Billy Bones knew him. Perhaps these papers will tell us about the treasure! Well done, Jim!”",
"We found a book of notes and a map. It was a map of ‘Treasure Island’. It showed a big hill called Spyglass Hill in the middle. There were three red crosses on the map. Next to the cross in the south west of the island were some words: ‘Most of the treasure is here.’",
"On the back of the map there was some more information: ‘Tall tree. Spyglass Hill. N. of N.N.E. Skeleton Island. E.S.E. by E. Ten Feet.’",
"Squire Trelawney was very excited. “I’ll go to Bristol tomorrow and buy a ship!” he said. “In three weeks we will have the best ship and the best crew in England. Jim will come with us as cabin boy. And you, Livesey, will be the ship’s doctor. We will find that treasure!”",
"“Trelawney,” said the doctor, “I’ll come with you. But there is one man I am afraid of.”",
"“Who?” cried the squire. “Tell me his name!”",
"“You,” said the doctor. “Because you cannot keep a secret. Nobody must know about this map.”",
"“You are right,” said the squire. “I will be as silent as the grave.”",
"But he was not. In Bristol he talked about the treasure to everybody: to the men who sold him the ship, to the sailors on the docks, to anyone who would listen. And so, in a few days, half the town knew that a ship was going to look for Captain Flint’s gold.",
"Three weeks later I said goodbye to my mother and to the cove and to dear old Admiral Benbow. The inn looked small and grey in the morning light, and I was suddenly sorry to leave it. Then I got into the coach for Bristol, and my adventure began."
],
4:[
"In Bristol, Squire Trelawney gave me a letter. “Take this to Long John Silver at the Spy-glass Inn,” he said. “He is our new ship’s cook.”",
"The Spy-glass was a small, bright inn near the docks. Behind the bar there was a tall, strong man with one leg. He moved quickly on a wooden crutch, and he had a green parrot on his shoulder. He smiled at me in a friendly way.",
"“You must be Jim Hawkins,” he said. “Welcome aboard! This is Captain Flint, my parrot. I called him that after the famous pirate.”",
"I liked him immediately. He was clean, intelligent and kind, and he talked to me like a man and not like a boy.",
"Then I looked at a man near the door — and I knew him. Two fingers were missing on his left hand.",
"“Oh!” I cried. “Stop him! It’s Black Dog!”",
"The man ran out of the door and disappeared into the street. Long John Silver shouted for help and sent three men after him. “Black Dog?” he said. “I don’t know the name. But nobody runs from my house without paying! Was he a friend of yours, Jim?”",
"He was so angry and so honest about it that I was sure he knew nothing.",
"A few days later we went on board the Hispaniola. Captain Smollett came to speak to the squire and the doctor.",
"“I don’t like this voyage,” he said. “I don’t like the crew, and I don’t like the fact that everybody in Bristol knows where we are going and why. There are men on this ship who know more about that map than I do.”",
"The squire was very angry, but the doctor listened. In the end they put the guns and the gunpowder under the cabin, and they said nothing more about the treasure.",
"We sailed. The voyage was long and hot. Long John Silver was the best man on the ship: he cooked, he sang, he mended clothes, and every sailor loved him. There was a barrel of apples on the deck, and any man could take one.",
"One evening, just before sunset, I wanted an apple. There were only a few left at the bottom, so I climbed inside the barrel to reach them. Then I sat down in the dark and fell asleep.",
"I woke up because somebody sat down against the barrel. It was Long John Silver, and he was talking to a young sailor.",
"“I sailed with Captain Flint,” he was saying quietly. “I was his quartermaster. Flint was afraid of nobody — and I was the only man he was afraid of.”",
"Then he explained his plan. He and his men — most of the crew — would let the captain find the treasure. Then, one night, they would kill the captain, the doctor, the squire and everybody who was not with them.",
"“And what about the honest men?” asked the young sailor.",
"“Dead men don’t talk,” said Long John Silver, in the same warm, friendly voice.",
"I was cold with fear inside the barrel. This kind, funny man was going to kill my friends.",
"Then a voice shouted from above: “Land ho!”"
],
5:[
"That evening I told Captain Smollett, Doctor Livesey and Squire Trelawney everything I had heard in the apple barrel.",
"“Jim,” said the captain, “you have saved our lives.” Then he counted. There were only seven honest men on the ship, including me. Against us there were nineteen pirates.",
"“We must say nothing,” said the doctor. “We must wait, and we must be ready.”",
"In the morning we saw Treasure Island. It was not beautiful. It was grey and wooded, with a big hill in the middle, and there was a smell of wet marsh in the hot air. Nobody felt happy when they looked at it.",
"The heat was terrible and there was no wind. The men were tired and angry, and they began to disobey. Captain Smollett had an idea: he gave the crew the afternoon on the island. Thirteen men went to the beach in the boats.",
"And then I did a mad thing. Without telling anybody, without asking permission, I jumped into one of the boats and went with them. When we reached the beach I ran into the trees as fast as I could.",
"I was on Treasure Island, alone, and nobody knew where I was. At first I was happy. I looked at strange plants and birds and I forgot about the pirates.",
"Then I heard voices. I hid behind a big tree and looked. Long John Silver was standing in the marsh with another sailor. The sailor was called Tom, and he was one of the honest men.",
"“Join us, Tom,” said Silver in his friendly voice. “Be a gentleman of fortune. There’s gold enough for everybody.”",
"“No,” said Tom. “I would rather lose my hand than break my word.”",
"At that moment we heard a terrible cry, far away in the marsh. Another honest sailor was dying.",
"“What was that?” said Tom. “That,” said Silver quietly, “that was Alan.”",
"“Alan!” cried Tom. “Then kill me too. You’ve killed him, and you can kill me. But you don’t frighten me.” And he turned his back on Silver and began to walk towards the beach.",
"Silver took his crutch in his hand. He threw it, and it hit Tom in the back. Tom fell. Before he could get up, Silver was on him with a knife — and Tom did not move again.",
"I could hardly breathe. I lay in the grass and watched Silver clean his knife on the grass. Then he took out a whistle and blew it, and I understood that other pirates were coming.",
"I got up and ran. I did not know where I was going. I only knew that I had to get away from that man."
],
6:[
"I ran for a long time. Then, suddenly, I stopped. Something was moving among the trees on the side of the hill.",
"It was a man — or something like a man. He ran from tree to tree like an animal, on two legs but bent almost double. He was coming towards me.",
"I did not know what to do. Behind me there were murderers. In front of me there was this strange creature. I decided that I preferred a wild man to Long John Silver, so I walked towards him.",
"He stopped and came out from behind a tree. His skin was burnt brown by the sun. His hair was long and wild. His clothes were made of goatskins and pieces of old sail, held together with brass buttons and bits of stick.",
"“Who are you?” I asked.",
"“Ben Gunn,” he answered, and his voice was strange and rusty, like a lock that nobody has opened for years. “I’m poor Ben Gunn, I am. Marooned three years agone, and lived on goats since then, and berries and oysters.”",
"“Three years!” I said. “Were you shipwrecked?”",
"“No, mate,” he said. “Marooned. They put me here and sailed away.” He looked at me carefully. “Now, tell me something. Do you have a piece of cheese about you? No? Many’s the long night I’ve dreamed of cheese — toasted, mostly — and woke up here again.”",
"I told him my name and my story, and he listened to every word. When I said the name of Long John Silver he became very frightened. But when I told him that we had Flint’s map, his eyes changed.",
"“I was on Flint’s ship when he buried the treasure,” he said. “He went ashore with six strong men and he came back alone. Nobody ever knew how he did it. Three years ago I was on another ship and we came to this island, and I told them about the gold. We looked for twelve days, and we found nothing. And on the twelfth day the men said to me, ‘You can stay here, Ben Gunn, and find it yourself.’ And they left me a spade and a gun, and they sailed away.”",
"He took my arm and looked at me with his strange bright eyes.",
"“Jim,” he said, “I’m rich. Rich, I tell you. And I’ll help you. But you must promise me something. You must ask your squire for a passage home — and a share. A fair share, mate, that’s all I ask.”",
"I did not understand what he meant about being rich. I thought that three years alone had made him a little mad. And then, far away over the trees, we heard the sound of a cannon.",
"“They have begun to fight,” I said. “Come with me, quickly!”"
],
7:[
"While I was on the island, my friends had left the ship. The doctor told me the story afterwards.",
"They took the small boat and went to an old wooden fort — a stockade — that Captain Flint had built years before, on a hill near a spring of fresh water. They carried food, gunpowder and medicine. The pirates saw them and fired the cannon, and the boat sank in shallow water, and they lost most of the food.",
"Redruth, the squire’s old servant, was shot and died that night. They buried him and put up the English flag over the log house.",
"“Why do you put up the flag?” asked the squire. “The pirates can see exactly where we are.”",
"“Let them see,” said Captain Smollett. “We are the lawful party, and I will not take our flag down.”",
"The pirates shot at the flag for an hour, and the captain laughed. “They are wasting powder,” he said.",
"The next morning a man came up the hill with a white cloth in his hand. It was Long John Silver.",
"“I have come to talk,” he called. “Give us the map, and we will let you live. You can come on board and go home to England, or you can stay here with food. That is my offer.”",
"“And that is all you get from me,” said Captain Smollett. “You cannot find the treasure. You cannot sail the ship. You cannot fight us — Mr Hands here has just proved that. You are in a bad position, Mr Silver, and you know it.”",
"Silver’s face went red with anger. “Give me a hand up,” he said. He was sitting on the sand, and with one leg he could not stand easily.",
"“Not I,” said the captain.",
"Silver pulled himself up on his crutch, spat into the spring, and went away down the hill.",
"An hour later the attack began. The pirates came running out of the trees on two sides, shouting. They climbed over the fence like monkeys and there was fighting inside the stockade — smoke, noise and men falling.",
"It did not last long. When the smoke cleared, five pirates were dead or dying, and the others were running back into the trees. But inside the log house, Captain Smollett was badly wounded, and two of our men were dead.",
"We had won — but there were only four of us who could still fight."
],
8:[
"That afternoon I did another mad thing.",
"I put two pistols in my pocket, filled my pockets with biscuits, and walked out of the stockade without telling anybody. I had a plan, and the plan was mine alone.",
"Ben Gunn had told me about a little boat that he had made with his own hands: a small round thing of goatskin over a frame of wood, hidden under a tent of goatskins on the beach. I found it as the sun went down.",
"When it was dark I carried the little boat to the water, and I paddled out to where the Hispaniola was lying at anchor. The pirates on board were singing and drinking. Nobody was watching.",
"I found the rope that held the ship — the hawser — and I cut it with my knife.",
"At once the ship began to move. Now the pirates had no ship at all: they could not leave the island, they could not take the treasure home, they could not do anything. And I had done it with a knife and a boat the size of a bath.",
"But then I understood something. The tide was going out, and it was taking me with it — out of the anchorage and into the open sea. The little boat turned round and round. I could not steer it at all. I could only sit still and hold on.",
"I passed the Hispaniola so close that I could hear the pirates fighting on board. Then the current carried me away into the dark.",
"It was a long, cold night. The waves were big and the little boat jumped over them like a cork. I was wet through and very frightened. In the end I was so tired that I fell asleep, and I dreamed of the Admiral Benbow and my mother.",
"When I woke up, the sun was shining. And there, half a mile away, was the Hispaniola — with all her sails up, moving slowly, and nobody at the wheel.",
"I paddled towards her. It was the most dangerous thing I have ever done, but I did not think about that. I only thought: that is our ship, and I am going to take her back."
],
9:[
"I climbed on board and jumped down onto the deck.",
"There were two men there. One was lying on his back, dead, with his arms out. The other was Israel Hands, the coxswain, sitting against the side of the ship. He was very pale, and there was blood on his leg, and there was an empty brandy bottle beside him.",
"“Well,” he said slowly, “here’s Jim Hawkins come on board. Come to visit, have you?”",
"“I have come to take command of this ship, Mr Hands,” I said. Then I took down the black pirate flag and threw it into the sea. “There are no more pirates here.”",
"He looked at me for a long time. “I want food and drink,” he said at last, “and a bit of cloth for my leg. And I’ll tell you how to sail her. There’s a good boy.”",
"So we made an agreement. I brought him brandy and food and bandages, and he told me how to steer the ship into the northern inlet where we could run her up safely on the sand.",
"He was very polite. He called me “Jim, my boy”, and he told me stories about the sea, and he asked me questions in a friendly voice. And all the time I did not trust him, because his eyes followed me everywhere I went.",
"When we were close to the shore he asked me to go below and bring him some wine. I said yes — but I did not go below. I ran up the mast and looked down through a crack in the deck.",
"And I saw Israel Hands get up. He crossed the deck quickly, without any pain at all, and he took a long knife out of the pile of stones at the bottom of the ship. He hid it inside his coat and went back to his place.",
"Now I knew everything. He could move. He had a knife. And when we reached the shore, he was going to kill me.",
"I came back with the wine and we talked as before. Then, suddenly, he threw the knife. It hit me in the shoulder and pinned me to the mast.",
"I do not remember pulling the trigger. My two pistols went off almost by themselves. Israel Hands cried out, let go of the ropes, and fell head first into the water. He did not come up again.",
"I sat on the mast with the blood running down my back, and I was sick, and frightened, and I could not stop shaking. There was no triumph in it at all."
],
10:[
"I brought the Hispaniola safely into the northern inlet and left her there on the sand. Then I walked back across the island in the dark, very pleased with myself, to tell my friends what I had done.",
"I saw the fire of the stockade and I walked in quietly to surprise them.",
"And a voice cried out in the darkness: “Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!”",
"It was Silver’s parrot. Somebody lit a torch — and I saw six pirates round the fire, and Long John Silver standing in the middle of them.",
"“So,” said Silver, “here’s Jim Hawkins. Come to join us, mate?”",
"One of the men stood up with a knife. “Let me finish him,” he said.",
"“Sit down,” said Silver, and he did not raise his voice. “This boy is worth more to me alive than dead. Nobody touches him.”",
"Then he explained to me, very calmly, what had happened. The doctor had given him the map. My friends had left the stockade. The pirates had taken it, and now they were going to look for the treasure — and I was their prisoner.",
"“I like you, Jim,” he said quietly, when the others were asleep. “You remind me of myself when I was young. Now listen. The doctor and the captain will hang me when this is over — unless somebody speaks for me. You save Long John from the rope, and Long John will save you from these men. Is it a bargain?”",
"It was not a kind offer. It was a business offer. But he had saved my life, and I gave him my word.",
"In the morning the other pirates were angry. They walked away and talked among themselves for a long time. Then one of them came back and put a piece of paper in Silver’s hand. It was a black circle, cut out with a knife, with one word written on it: ‘Deposed’.",
"Silver looked at it and laughed. “Where did you get the paper?” he asked. “Why, you’ve cut this out of a Bible! What fool cut a Bible?”",
"The men went white. To cut a Bible was terrible bad luck, worse than any black spot, and they knew it. In one minute Silver had turned their own judgement into a joke, and they were frightened again — of him, and of the sky.",
"Later that morning Doctor Livesey came up the hill to the fort, with medicine in his bag. He treated every wounded pirate, one after the other, without saying a word about what they had done.",
"Then he asked to speak to me alone.",
"“Jim,” he said quietly, “run. Come with me now.”",
"“I can’t,” I said. “I gave Silver my word.”",
"The doctor looked at me for a long moment. “Then keep it,” he said."
],
11:[
"The next morning we all went to look for the treasure. Silver put a rope round my waist and held the other end in his hand, and I walked in front of him all day like a dancing bear at a fair.",
"We followed the directions on the map. Soon one of the men shouted. Under a tall tree there was a skeleton, lying straight on the ground with its arms above its head, pointing like a compass.",
"“That’s Flint’s work,” said Silver quietly. “Six men he took ashore, and six men he killed. And then he used one of them for a pointer.” The pirates looked at each other and said nothing.",
"We walked on towards the tall tree. And then, out of the trees, came a thin high voice, singing: “Fifteen men on the dead man’s chest — Yo-ho-ho and a bottle of rum!”",
"The pirates stopped. Their faces went grey. “It’s Flint!” one of them whispered. “It’s Flint’s ghost!”",
"“Ghost or no ghost,” said Silver, “I came here for the gold, and I’m not going back for any voice in a tree.” Then he listened again, and I saw him smile. “Wait,” he said. “That’s not Flint. That’s a living man — and I know his voice. That’s Ben Gunn!”",
"The men were still afraid, but they walked on, and at last we came to the tall tree on the map.",
"There, in the ground, was a great hole.",
"It was empty. There was nothing in it but a broken pickaxe and some old boards from packing cases. The treasure had gone — and it had gone a long time ago.",
"For a moment nobody spoke. Then the pirates jumped down into the hole and began to dig with their hands, and when they found nothing they turned round and looked at Long John Silver with murder in their faces.",
"And at that moment three shots came out of the trees. Two pirates fell, and the others ran. Doctor Livesey, Ben Gunn and Abraham Gray came out of the wood with their guns in their hands.",
"“Thank you, doctor,” said Silver calmly. “You came in time, I think.”",
"Then they told me the whole story. Ben Gunn had found the treasure two years before, alone. Little by little, over many weeks, he had carried it on his back to a cave on the north side of the island. That was why the doctor had given Silver the map: the map was worthless, and he knew it.",
"We spent three days carrying the gold from Ben Gunn’s cave to the Hispaniola: English, French, Spanish and Portuguese coins, and gold pieces from countries I had never heard of. I was kept busy packing the money into bread bags, and my back hurt, and I have never seen anything so beautiful or so boring.",
"We left three pirates on the island with food and tools, because we could not take them home to be hanged.",
"On the voyage home, at a port in America, Long John Silver disappeared in the night. He took one bag of coins with him — about four hundred pounds — and nobody ever heard of him again. I was not sorry.",
"Ben Gunn got his thousand pounds and spent it all in nineteen days, which was exactly what everybody expected. The squire, the doctor and Captain Smollett all had their share.",
"And I have my share too. But I have never gone back to that island, and I never will. Sometimes, in the worst of my dreams, I hear a sharp voice in the dark: “Pieces of eight! Pieces of eight!”"
],
};

